    "summary": "Chest [a] of red cedar wood, with lid [b]. The sides are made of one piece of wood cut or kerfed on the inside, shaved on the outside, and steamed and bent to form three corners, the fourth corner being fitted together and pegged with red cedar pegs. The base is also pegged to the sides. The lid, a flat piece of wood larger than the box is fitted into the chest on the underside, and juts out slightly above the box, the profile of the lid being a parallelogram. The box is unpainted and signed on the bottom in incised lines &#039;Ray Martin&#039;.",
